+# Uptime development notes
+
+- The original code reproduced a one-read shutdown decision: fresh read true,
+  injected PermissionError false, next fresh read true. Historical live shutdown
+  causes remain unproved because original stop reasons were not retained.
+- The first local regression run after the correction failed the old child-process
+  fixture: it supplied one frozen heartbeat and bypassed only the old boolean
+  helper. The corrected persistent guard correctly expired that receipt. The
+  test fixture now supplies synthetic progressing heartbeat timestamps and runs
+  the actual guard; test acquisition assertions were not reduced.
+- An intermediate test-module import exposed the original RuntimeTests class to
+  unittest a second time. That duplicate discovery was removed. The final
+  counted suite has 177 distinct test IDs: 40 uptime tests and 137 regressions.
+- Intermediate logs are retained. The final result has zero failures/errors/skips.
+- No Windows runtime, actual Schwab credentials/provider calls, installation or
+  production journal access is claimed by these local results. The test report
+  records Python 3.13.5 and exchange_calendars 4.13.1 on Linux; the operator's
+  closeout-qa environment remains unchanged and will report its own versions.
